Z||000026||862M4inCA||01-27-2000||06:19 PM||||Will, That is with a stock 2.5 and 5 sp. I've done nothing to the car since I purchased it in april of last year aside from a new clutch and cylinder head. As I recall, I was at about 3000 RPM when my speedo was pointing straight down. Again I only have my sisters verification for the 95 MPH reading. I have however been wanting to pick up a 120 MPH speedo to verify this info, and a nice long street to see what this 2.5 is capable of. ||||reg||1
Z||000027||CUTTER||01-27-2000||10:48 PM||||I got my 87GT stock except for flowmasters past the 120 mark on the spedo. I figured it out to be around 130-132. Good for a 2.8 almost stock!||||reg||1
Z||000028||Standard||01-28-2000||02:07 AM||||I agree with Will.  Top speed is the point where you're car doesn't have enough power to overcome the wind resistance.  I'm sure if you cleaned your car up good, took off anything that cause turbulance you could eke out a few more mph's..||||reg||1
Z||000029||WKDFIRO||01-28-2000||02:34 AM||||Phil, I inadvertantly did that but I found out a funny thing...<P>When you suck the doors off a CHP on the freeway doing around 110 (I hadn't done my 120 speedo mod yet)radar can't lock on you fast enough. I had gotten out of the gas by the time he caught up with me. I am so surprised that I wasn't kissing my hood with my hands behind my back. The cop said that his radar couldn't lock on fast enough but he did have to go to 105 just to start to catch up...he asked me how fast I was going. I looked down at my speedo and looked back up at him and squeaked "80?" I know if I had said, "I don't know" than he would have given me whatever number he wanted. He put 80++ on my ticket and told me that he would be there if I fought the ticket.<P>I ate the $247 fine knowing that it should have been MUCH worse.....<P>Ah....the days when I was Young and Immortal....<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-28-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000030||chris6878||01-28-2000||12:34 PM||||this wind resistence you guys are talking of...   i am a college student and had physic's last semester...    and what if you had a "tail wind"   (one blowing the same direction your are going), according to my studies, that would make your go faster....  hmmm...       but i cant remember the equation...  so dont ask   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">        i guess thats why i made a "C" in the class..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>chris||||reg||3
Z||000031||WGraffiKs||01-31-2000||09:37 PM||||Yes, Chris, a tail wind effectively subtracts from wind resistance from the front.  So if you had a tail wind of, say...125mph, and your Fiero could go 125 with no wind, College physics says that you can now go 250MPH!!!  Which is great until the wind shifts 90 degrees, and blows you laterally into the next state!  Usually happens just as you suck the doors off of a CHP cruiser, too. ;}||||reg||1
Z||000032||Phaeton||02-01-2000||05:10 AM||||I did the radar trick with my foot all the way into it..127 mph.  The officer did not congratulate me for having fine auto ?!? and no license for ninety days was the judge's opinion!!  That was stock 2.8, flat road and about 40 degrees f.||||reg||1
